  "solution": {
    "text": "Energy released, when electron is added in outer most shell of isolated gaseous atom or ions is called electron affinity. <math> <mrow> <mtext>Electron</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>affinity</mtext><mo>∝</mo><mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>Nuclear</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>charge</mtext></mrow> <mrow> <mtext>Radius</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>of</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>atoms/ions</mtext></mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>Li</mtext> <mo>+</mo> </msup> <mo>+</mo> <mn>1</mn> <msup> <mtext>e</mtext> <mo>-</mo> </msup> <mo>→</mo>&nbsp; </mrow> </math>Attraction<br /><math> <mrow>  <msup>   <mrow>    <mtext>Li</mtext></mrow>   <mtext>+</mtext>  </msup>  <mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>&#x003E;</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><msup>   <mrow>    <mtext>Na</mtext></mrow>   <mtext>+</mtext>  </msup>  </mrow></math> electron can reach more nearer to nucleus &amp; Energy released will be highest."
